# State Management Rules

- Use the state-management solution selected by `/flutter/docs/04-state-management.md`; do not introduce a competing state framework casually.
- Separate server/domain state from transient UI state.
- Represent loading, success, error, stale, and sync-pending states explicitly where necessary.
- Avoid global mutable singletons for business state.
- Do not duplicate authoritative delivery state in multiple unrelated controllers.
- State should be derived from repository/application data whenever possible.
- Keep side effects out of pure state/model objects.
